{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The root cause was in `repo/version.py`: `compare_versions` was comparing the version strings directly with `<`/`>`, which does a lexical (character-by-character) comparison. Lexically, `\"1.10.0\" < \"1.9.0\"` is `True` because `'1' < '9'` at the second character — so the updater wrongly treated `1.9.0` as newer than `1.10.0`.\n\nThe fix splits each version on `.` into a tuple of ints (`_parse`) and compares those tuples numerically, padding shorter tuples with `0` so versions like `1.9` and `1.9.0` compare equal. Both `test_double_digit_minor` and `test_major_bump` now pass."}]},"session_id":"cbf14b6a-a0db-4101-bfd9-e95d0207827b"}
